<urn:atm:triage:finding/AY14-QA-003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AY14-QA-003" ;
  triage:title "ensure_canonical_member_name_available never checks other members' alias field and skips the caller's own team, so a plain add whose canonical name collides with an existing member's alias is silently accepted" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr, raised directly by Rand 2026-09-07: 'atm must reject any team member add that will not work on herdr. We added alias so this would work. alias MUST meet herdr requirements for uniqueness. alias (if missing) would default to team member name.' This restates AC7/AC8 (docs/plans/phase-ay/sprint-AY.14-herdr-agent-name-mapping.md lines 118-162, 231-269): every roster member's effective Herdr identity is its alias if set, else its own canonical agent_name, and that identity must be unique database-wide. crates/atm-core/src/team_admin/member_mutation.rs implements this asymmetrically. ensure_alias_available(roster_store, alias) (lines ~456-472), invoked whenever an explicit alias is given, correctly checks the candidate alias against every other member's agent_name AND metadata_json['alias'] fields, across all teams -- this direction is correct. ensure_canonical_member_name_available(roster_store, team, member) (lines ~486-506), invoked only when NO alias is given (add_member: 'if request.alias.is_none()'; update_member: 'if request.alias == Some(None)'), only compares the candidate canonical name against other teams' agent_name field -- it never inspects any other member's metadata_json['alias'] field, and it explicitly skips the caller's own team ('if conflicting_team == *team { continue; }'). Concrete failure: member X is added with alias 'bob' (X's own canonical agent_name is something else, e.g. 'member-42'), claiming Herdr identity 'bob'. A later add-member call for a plain member literally named 'bob' with no --alias is currently ACCEPTED with no error, producing two roster rows that both resolve to the identical HerdrAgentName 'bob' -- resolve_herdr_agent_target (crates/atm-core/src/delivery_channel.rs:119) is a stateless per-member function with no roster-wide visibility and cannot detect this at delivery time; no downstream dedup exists in herdr_queue_wake.rs, replacement_handler.rs, or doctor/report.rs either. Confirmed pre-existing (not introduced by the AY.14/PR #1305 diff -- `git diff $(git merge-base HEAD integrate/phase-ay)..HEAD -- crates/atm-core/src/team_admin/member_mutation.rs` shows zero changes to either function). Rand independently confirmed the exact target behavior via a 3-case matrix: (a) member='bob', alias='bobby' -> accepted [already correct: alias check skipped when alias unset is false; ensure_alias_available('bobby') finds no conflict]; (b) member='robert', alias='bob' colliding with X's alias -> rejected [already correct: ensure_alias_available checks metadata_json['alias'] db-wide]; (c) member='bob', no alias, colliding with X's alias -> must be rejected, currently is NOT [this gap]. Required correction: extend ensure_canonical_member_name_available (or fold it into a single symmetric check shared with ensure_alias_available) to also reject when the candidate canonical name matches any other member's metadata_json['alias'] value, database-wide, including the caller's own team (the same-team skip has no basis under AC7's database-wide scope), plus a regression test driving this exact ordering (alias claimed first, colliding plain name added second) through both add-member and update-member paths." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ay" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "requirements-compliance" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-core/src/team_admin/member_mutation.rs (ensure_canonical_member_name_available, ensure_alias_available, load_member_add_context, update_member_with_roster_store)" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-07T20:05:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AY14 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-07T19:40:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AY14-QA-003/1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

